{"name":"Ansel","hex":"#016884","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ansel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A male given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ansel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ansel Adams Wilderness","blocks":[{"text":"The Ansel Adams Wilderness is a wilderness area in the Sierra Nevada of California, United States. The wilderness spans 231,533 acres (93,698 ha); 33.9% of the territory lies in the Inyo National Forest, 65.8% is in the Sierra National Forest, and the remaining 0.3% covers nearly all of Devils Postpile National Monument. Yosemite National Park lies to the north and northwest, while the John Muir Wilderness lies to the south."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Mt_Banner_and_Thousand_Island_Lake.jpg/330px-Mt_Banner_and_Thousand_Island_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ansel_Adams_Wilderness","wikidata":"Q569492"},{"title":"Ansel (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Ansel is a name derived from the same root as Anselm, a medieval Germanic name of uncertain meaning, perhaps view 'follower of a nobleman' or 'with divine protection'. \nNotable people with the name include:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ansel_(name)","wikidata":"Q65119566"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Panoramaanseladams.jpg/500px-Panoramaanseladams.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Panoramaanseladams.jpg/1280px-Panoramaanseladams.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Panoramaanseladams.jpg/500px-Panoramaanseladams.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ansel Adams Wilderness","link":"https://en.wikipe